  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1952-p20.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Set \\(x=3k\\) and \\(y=4k.\\) The first four expressions become \\(\\frac{7}{4},\\) \\(4,\\) \\(\\frac{11}{3},\\) and \\(\\frac{3}{8},\\) respectively. But \\[ \\frac{x-y}{y}=\\frac{3k-4k}{4k}=-\\frac14, \\] not \\(\\frac{1}{4}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Let \\(x=3k\\) and \\(y=4k\\)",
        "Pay attention to the sign of \\(x-y\\)"
      ],
